    "updated_at": "2023-01-18T02:42:36Z",
    "body": "```\r\nA navigable presents a [Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#document) to the user via its [active session history entry](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#nav-active-history-entry). Each navigable has:\r\n\r\nAn id, a [new unique internal value](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#new-unique-internal-value).\r\n\r\nA parent, a [navigable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigable) or null.\r\n\r\nA current session history entry, a [session history entry](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#session-history-entry).\r\n\r\nThis can only be modified within the [session history traversal queue](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#tn-session-history-traversal-queue) of the parent [traversable navigable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#traversable-navigable).\r\n\r\nAn active session history entry, a [session history entry](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#session-history-entry).\r\n\r\nThis can only be modified from the event loop of the [active session history entry](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#nav-active-history-entry)'s [document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#she-document).\r\n\r\nAn is closing boolean, initially false.\r\n\r\nThis is only ever set to true for [top-level traversable navigables](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#top-level-traversable).\r\n\r\nAn is delaying load events boolean, initially false.\r\n\r\nThis is only ever set to true in cases where the navigable's [parent](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#nav-parent) is non-null.\r\n```\r\n\r\nHonestly I'm even more confused after reading this. No Document is presented by it, so what makes it a navigable? This seems to list out the properties of a navigable without actually saying conceptually what it is.",
