    "updated_at": "2023-01-18T03:14:18Z",
    "body": "You're misunderstanding. When you are viewing a document with a `<a href=\"tel:...\">` link, that is the document being presented in the navigable (~= browser tab). That navigable then gets navigated to the `tel:...` URL via the \"follow a hyperlink\" steps I linked above.\r\n\r\nAs for conceptual vs. definitions, this is a specification, so we tend toward the latter. I think the immediately-preceding section https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents gives a more conceptual overview, but the intended audience is still browser vendors implementing a browser.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
